WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:02.190
ANTHONY BUSHONG:
Today we're talking

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:05.100
about the future of data,
mosquitoes, and tick data

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:06.190
analytics.

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:08.670
I'm Anthony, and welcome
to This Week in Cloud,

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:12.120
where we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:14.070
Numerous factors
underpin the challenges

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:16.920
of growing data volume,
including access and storage,

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:21.210
inconsistent tools, new and
evolving sources and formats,

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:24.990
compliance concerns, and
security considerations.

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:27.610
To help you identify and
solve these challenges,

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:29.910
we've created a new
whitepaper, "The future

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:32.820
of data will be unified,
flexible, and accessible,"

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:35.760
which explores many of the most
common reasons our customers

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.700
tell us they're choosing Google
Cloud to get the most out

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.650
of their data.

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:43.020
Mosquitoes aren't just the
peskiest creatures on Earth.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:45.570
They infect more than
700 million people a year

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:49.230
with dangerous diseases, like
Zika, malaria, dengue fever,

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:50.730
and yellow fever.

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:52.860
Prevention is the
best protection,

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:54.990
and stopping mosquito
bites before they happen

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:56.980
is a critical step.

00:00:56.980 --> 00:00:58.440
That's why Google
Cloud was honored

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:00.398
to team up with one of
the leading pest control

00:01:00.398 --> 00:01:02.940
brands, OFF!, to
develop a new publicly

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:05.820
available predictive model
of when and where mosquito

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:08.760
populations are
emerging nationwide.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:12.480
Learn more about the mosquito
forecast on the blog.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:14.400
We just published the
blog post announcing

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:18.300
Google Cloud's latest
STAC-M3 benchmark results.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:21.810
Following up on our 2018
STAC-M3 benchmark audit,

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:23.730
a redesigned Google
Cloud architecture

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:25.920
achieved significant
improvements-- up

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:29.340
to 18 times faster, up to
9 times higher throughput,

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:30.480
and more.

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:32.880
Read more about these
results and a whitepaper

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:35.220
on how we designed and
optimized the cluster

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:39.117
for API-driven cloud
resources on the blog.

00:01:39.117 --> 00:01:41.200
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.370
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:44.650
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:44.650 --> 00:01:46.490
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:48.660
We'll see you in the cloud.

